{"c":[{"name":"20261002T201045Z-88beaae782960744","text":"Never edit a running bash script in place (bash reads it as it runs); write a new file and mv it over, as B6 did with run-audit.sh mid-audit.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261002T201045Z-f95178d8fbcf4b52","text":"ScreenModel.apply builds a new WindowState and nodes Map per snapshot; candidates.ts and descriptor.ts cache per-state indexes in WeakMaps, so never mutate w.nodes in place.","type":"note"}]}
